        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">A home treadmill beats a mid-priced gym membership on money</strong>
            within roughly one and a half to three years for a regular user, faster for a
            household and faster again if you sell it later. Against a budget gym, or a gym you
            would keep for weights, it does not.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The deciding variable is use, not price. Prove the routine for eight weeks first, then
            buy a mid-range machine without a mandatory subscription and keep it
            <a href="/treadmill-maintenance-cost/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">maintained</a>
            — at that point the cardio is close to free.
          </p>
